{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaL1Ceiling","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaL1Ceiling","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chirality_sum_below_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chirality_sum_below_target","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaL1Ceiling.lean#L70-L78","doc":"**Chirality specialization.**  A genuine sign function (`s i = ±1`)\nsatisfies `|s i| ≤ 1`, so the prune applies to ANY chirality rule\nreplacing the proven `sgn(w₀^{S_{λ'}})`.  This is the exact statement\nused by the Δ_λ ℓ¹-ceiling prune. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weighted_sum_below_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weighted_sum_below_target","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaL1Ceiling.lean#L59-L68","doc":"**Sign-only prune.**  If the ℓ¹ ceiling `∑ |a i|` is strictly below the\ntarget magnitude `T`, then NO bounded weight reassignment reaches `T`:\n`|∑ s i * a i| < T` for every `s` with `|s i| ≤ 1`.  With\n`a := y_λ χ^λ dim_λ` and `s` the chirality sign, this is the structural\nexclusion behind the Δ_λ prune (the witness measures\n`∑ |a i| / T ∈ [0.36, 0.59] < 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_weighted_sum_le_l1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.abs_weighted_sum_le_l1","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaL1Ceiling.lean#L42-L57","doc":"**ℓ¹ ceiling.**  For per-block magnitude carriers `a : ι → R` and any\nper-block weight `s : ι → R` bounded by `1` in absolute value (in\nparticular any chirality sign `s i = ±1`), the weighted sum is bounded\nin absolute value by the ℓ¹ norm `∑ |a i|`, for **every** `s`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}